---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AssignmentIdentity from "../../components/AssignmentIdentity.astro";
import { external } from "../../data/site";
import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";
const proposal = readFileSync("assignments/assignment-3/proposal/dataset.md", "utf8");
const proposalValue = (label: string) => {
  const row = proposal.split("\n").find((line) => line.startsWith(`| ${label} |`));
  if (!row) throw new Error(`Missing proposal summary field: ${label}`);
  return row.split("|")[2].trim();
};
---
<BaseLayout title="Assignment 3" description="N24News image–text classification: six-category M1 proposal, preliminary metadata evidence, and planned fusion experiments." current="a3">
  <section class="shell page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Assignment 3 · Image–text classification</p>
    <div class="page-status"><span class="status status-planned">M1 proposal available</span><small>Pending instructor approval</small></div>
    <h1>Headlines and images,<br />one news category.</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">A six-category N24News proposal comparing image-only, headline-only, and fusion models on original article–image pairs.</p>
    <div class="button-row"><a class="button" href={external.a3Proposal}>Read Dataset Proposal ↗</a><a class="text-link" href={external.a3Ai}>Read AI disclosure ↗</a></div>
  </section>
  <AssignmentIdentity />
  <section class="shell article-layout">
    <article>
      <div class="notice"><strong>M1 proposal record · Pending instructor approval.</strong><p>Preliminary metadata and an 18-pair visual review are available. Training-use permission is not cleared; student verification, full image validation, and instructor approval remain pending. No main experiments have begun.</p></div>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Problem statement</h2>
        <p>Classify an original news headline and its associated RGB image into Food, Health, Science, Sports, Technology, or Travel. The prediction unit is one article–image pair. Image–text classification is explicitly listed in handbook Section 26.</p>
        <p>The project will examine whether images help short or ambiguous headlines and when their evidence conflicts. Only the headline is supplied as text; article bodies, captions, abstracts, URLs, filenames, and category metadata are excluded from model inputs.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Dataset description and EDA</h2>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/billywzh717/N24News">N24News</a> pairs news text and images from The New York Times. The proposal pins source revision <a href="https://github.com/billywzh717/N24News/tree/047a2bc3f4df0ea738b847a4ac3a6bd6aa2e4106"><code>047a2bc</code></a> and the JSON checksum.</p>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Pinned metadata findings · image validation pending</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Finding</th><th scope="col">Count</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td>Full source records / categories</td><td>{proposalValue("Full metadata records / categories")}</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Source records in selected categories</td><td>{proposalValue("Records across selected categories")}</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Distinct image URLs / raw headlines</td><td>{proposalValue("Distinct image URLs / raw headlines")}</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Candidate representatives after duplicate filtering</td><td>{proposalValue("Candidate representatives after filtering")}</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Metadata-selected pairs / categories</td><td>{proposalValue("Metadata-selected pairs / categories")}</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Train / validation / test targets</td><td>{proposalValue("Train / validation / test targets")}</td></tr>
        </tbody></table></div>
        <p>Every selected category starts with 3,000 source records; selection targets 1,250 per category. There are no empty headlines or image URLs in the 18,000 source records, and median headline length is nine whitespace-delimited words. The <a href={external.a3Proposal}>proposal</a> summarizes the findings, exclusions, selection rules, and limitations.</p>
        <p>The preliminary visual review decoded {proposalValue("Decoded sample pairs")} training pairs, three per category. AI-assisted assessments: {proposalValue("Visual sample assessments")}. This small sample does not estimate the full dataset's mismatch rate. Student verification remains pending; the <a href={external.a3Proposal}>proposal</a> records the method and limitations.</p>
        <p>The decoded sample contains 17 JPEG images and one PNG. All 18 have publisher/year overlays, and some contain additional text. Inspect these artifacts after preprocessing before freezing the experiment protocol. Images, headlines, and contact sheets remain ignored local review files.</p>
        <p><strong>Usage terms remain unresolved; training permission is not cleared.</strong> The official repository declares no standalone dataset license. The <a href="https://help.nytimes.com/115014893428-Terms-of-Service">publisher's terms, §§2.1 and 4.1</a>, require prior written consent for the listed ML/AI development uses; none has been supplied. Academic/non-commercial status is not itself a grant. If permission will not be obtained, replace N24News before main experiments.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Methodology</h2>
        <p>Use RGB images resized/cropped to 224×224 with ImageNet normalization, and original headlines tokenized with DistilBERT at a maximum of 64 tokens with attention masks. Both inputs come from the same source article record. Keep both pretrained encoders frozen in evaluation mode and train only heads, projections, and gates.</p>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Planned models · no training performed</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Configuration</th><th scope="col">Method</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td>Image only</td><td>ImageNet ResNet-18, 512-dimensional features, six-class head</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Text only</td><td>DistilBERT, masked mean-pooled 768-dimensional features, six-class head</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Simple fusion</td><td>Concatenated frozen features and 256-unit ReLU MLP</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Improved fusion</td><td>256-dimensional modality projections with learned gated weighting</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Gate ablation</td><td>Same projections/classifier with equal fixed modality weights</td></tr>
        </tbody></table></div>
        <p>Each configuration uses supervised cross-entropy. Train unimodal heads separately, then fusion heads on the same frozen encoder features. Backbone fine-tuning is outside the core scope. Missing raw modalities exclude a pair from the primary benchmark; diagnostic modality removal is reported separately.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Experimental setup</h2>
        <p>Build connected components using exact article URLs, exact image URLs, or normalized headlines. Exclude conflicting-label components and retain one representative per remaining group. Rank candidates by SHA-256 of <code>42|article_url</code>; select 1,250 per category and assign 1,000/125/125 to training/validation/test. The current targets are <strong>6,000 / 750 / 750</strong>.</p>
        <p>Before training, check selected images for availability, decoding, exact/perceptual duplicates, semantic alignment, and repeated events. Record exclusions and any regrouping, then freeze a revised deterministic manifest. Known repeated records/events stay together. Metadata alone cannot guarantee event independence.</p>
        <p>Initial settings: AdamW, learning rate 0.001, weight decay 0.0001, batch size 32, and at most 20 epochs per configuration. Reset seed 42 for each run. Select by validation macro-F1, then lower validation loss and earlier epoch. Reserve test evaluation until selection is complete.</p>
        <p>Planning estimate: approximately 8 GB GPU memory, 10 GB free storage, and 1–3 GPU-hours including feature extraction. Confirm actual hardware and pilot runtime after prerequisites. Record exact dependencies, pretrained revisions, configs, logs, run IDs, checkpoint hashes, and commit/tag.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Results</h2>
        <p>No experimental results are available at M1. Planned outputs include accuracy, macro-F1, per-class metrics, confusion matrices, learning curves, qualitative examples, parameter counts, feature-extraction/head-training times, inference latency, and peak memory. Dataset statistics above are preliminary metadata findings.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Comparison and discussion</h2>
        <p>Compare image-only and text-only baselines with concatenation and gated fusion. The gate ablation isolates adaptive versus equal weighting using the same projected representations and classifier design. State hypotheses, changed/fixed factors, validation decision criteria, capacity differences, and compute costs. Fusion is not assumed to outperform either modality.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Error analysis</h2>
        <p>After execution, report cases where both modalities support the label, one rescues the other, or their predictions conflict. Examine ambiguous headlines, illustrative images, Science/Technology confusion, overlapping editorial categories, and repeated events. Include example counts and diagnostic modality removal without treating gate values as causal proof.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Limitations and conclusion</h2>
        <p>The scope is six editorial categories from one English-language publisher, headline-only text, frozen encoders, and one seed. Metadata deduplication and the small visual sample cannot establish full-dataset semantic agreement, detect every repeated event, or prove all images valid. The 7,500-pair selection remains provisional until full image checks.</p>
        <p>The proposal and preliminary visual findings are available for review. Student verification, full image/pair validation, submission, and instructor approval remain pending. Training-use permission is not cleared; no grant or completed licensing compliance is claimed. M1 is due 18 November, M2 on 25 November, and M3 on 2 December 2026, each at 23:59 GMT+7.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Assignment-specific AI Usage Disclosure</h2>
        <p>OpenAI Codex assisted with N24News research, duplicate-aware selection, the image–text proposal/experiment plan, and public records. Metadata and publisher terms were checked, and 18 decoded pairs were visually inspected by Codex; student verification remains pending. The earlier task's disclosure is retained as superseded history. <a href={external.a3Ai}>Read the complete Assignment 3 log.</a></p>
      </section>
    </article>
    <aside class="side-stack"><section class="resource-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Resources</p><h2>Deliverables</h2>
      <a class="resource-link" href={external.a3Proposal}><span>Dataset proposal</span><b>Open ↗</b></a>
      <div class="pending">Pending instructor approval</div>
      <a class="resource-link" href={external.a3Readme}><span>M1 README</span><b>Open ↗</b></a>
      <a class="resource-link" href={external.a3Ai}><span>AI disclosure</span><b>Open ↗</b></a>
      <div class="pending">Training source code · pending prerequisites</div>
      <div class="pending">Checkpoints / reconstruction · pending implementation</div>
      <div class="pending">Final report · pending</div>
      <div class="pending">Slides · pending</div>
      <div class="pending">YouTube video · pending</div>
    </section></aside>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
